{
  "case_id": "2022-21-869",
  "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 2016, petitioner Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visual Arts, Inc. (AWF) licensed to Cond\u00e9 Nast for $10,000 an image of \u201cOrange Prince\u201d\u2014an orange silkscreen portrait of the musician Prince created by pop artist Andy Warhol\u2014to appear on the cover of a magazine commemorating Prince."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goldsmith",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Goldsmith notifed AWF of her belief that it had infringed her copyright."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visual Arts, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "AWF contends that the Prince Series works are \u201ctransformative,\u201d and that the frst fair use factor thus weighs in AWF's favor, because the works convey a different meaning or message than the photograph."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "AWF came away with $10,000. Goldsmith received nothing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The frst factor favors Goldsmith, not AWF."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court granted summary judgment for AWF."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visual Arts, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "AWF contends that the Prince Series works are \u201ctransformative,\u201d and that the frst factor therefore weighs in its favor, because the works convey a different meaning or message than the photograph."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0001-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the context of the challenged use, the frst fair use factor still favors Goldsmith."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The undisputed commercial character of AWF's use, though not dispositive, \u201ctends to weigh against a fnding of fair use.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just as Goldsmith licensed her photograph to Vanity Fair for $400, AWF licensed Orange Prince to Cond\u00e9 Nast for $10,000."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The use also \u201cis of a commercial nature.\u201d \u00a7 107(1)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0003-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The dissent contends that the Court gives \u201clittle role\u201d to \u201cthe key term `character.' \u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The purpose of Campbell's logo is to advertise soup. Warhol's canvases do not share that purpose. Rather, the Soup Cans series uses Campbell's copyrighted work for an artistic commentary on consumerism, a purpose that is orthogonal to advertising soup."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andy Warhol Foundation for Visual Arts, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "AWF contends, however, that the purpose and character of its use of Goldsmith's photograph weighs in favor of fair use because Warhol's silkscreen image of the photograph, like the Campbell's Soup Cans series, has a new meaning or message."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court determined that \u201c[t]he Prince Series works can reasonably be perceived to have transformed Prince from a vulnerable, uncomfortable person to an iconic, larger-than-life fgure.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andy Warhol Foundation for Visual Arts, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "AWF asserts another, albeit related, purpose, which is to comment on the \u201cdehumanizing nature\u201d and \u201ceffects\u201d of celebrity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here, the circumstances of AWF's 2016 licensing outweigh its diminished claim to fairness in copying under the frst factor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The dissent wonders: Why does targeting matter?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0004-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because this Court agrees with the Court of Appeals that the frst factor likewise favors her, the judgment of the Court of Appeals is Affrmed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0004-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Andy Warhol created 16 works based on Lynn Goldsmith's photograph: 14 silkscreen prints and two pencil drawings. The works are collectively known as the Prince Series."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0004-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question before us is a narrow one of statutory interpretation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Andy Warhol Foundation for Visual Arts, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On the Foundation's telling, the statute requires courts to focus on the purpose the creator had in mind when producing his work and the character of his resulting work. So what matters in this case is that Andy Warhol intended to apply a \u201c `new aesthetic' \u201d to Lynn Goldsmith's photograph and the character of his work \u201c `transformed' \u201d Prince from the \u201c `vulnerable, uncomfortable person' \u201d depicted in Ms. Goldsmith's photograph into \u201c `an iconic, larger-than-life fgure.' \u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0006-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "use that adds something new and important\u201d as \u201ctransformative.\u201d Ibid. We reiterated that protecting transformative uses \u201cstimulate[s] creativity\u201d and thus \u201cfulfll[s] the objective of copyright law.\u201d Ibid. (quoting Leval 1111)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0006-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "From top to bottom, the analysis fails. It does not ft the copyright statute. It is not faithful to our precedent. And it does not serve the purpose both Congress and the Court have understood to lie at the core of fair use: \u201cstimulat[ing] creativity,\u201d by enabling artists and writers of every descrip- tion to build on prior works."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-869",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "e30b7422927af494ce2dd0c56261138e27bc03f6e4bdfd13aaf654cc53564c6d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e30b7422927a-0006-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "courts are supposed to strike a balance between the two\u2014 and thus between rewarding original creators and enabling others to build on their works."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
